@startuml feature_v4_F-001_sequence
' Runtime truth for F-001 v4 — Service onboarding pipeline
' The cast below is the `participants:` list of feature_v4_F-001_front-matter.yaml, name for name.
' One group per story; one group per failure mode the front matter declares.
title F-001 v4 — Service onboarding pipeline
autonumber

actor "Requester" as Requester
participant "service-seed CLI" as CLI
participant "jira_intake" as Intake
participant "service_template" as Template
participant "gitops_pr" as GitOps
participant "Issue tracker" as Tracker
participant "Source host" as SourceHost
database "Cluster registry" as Registry
database "Tier profiles" as Profiles

group F-001-US1 — one tracker request is read once into one agreed description
  Requester -> CLI : seed-from-jira --jira-issue-key {issueKey}
  CLI -> CLI : read the two credential variables from the environment by name
  CLI -> Tracker : GET rest/api/3/issue/{issueKey}
  Tracker --> CLI : tracker-native issue
  CLI -> Intake : parse_service_request(issue, overrides)
  Intake -> Intake : __post_init__ checks issue type, issue key, service name, slug, SLO class
  Intake --> CLI : frozen service_request
end

group F-001-US2 — an unusable request is refused immediately, naming the field
  CLI -> Intake : parse_service_request(issue, overrides)
  Intake --> CLI : JiraIntakeError carrying the offending field
  CLI --> Requester : error: invalid Jira intake (field=...), exit 2, nothing created
end

group F-001-US3 — the service repository is created and seeded from the standard template
  CLI -> GitOps : create_repository(service_slug, project_key)
  GitOps -> SourceHost : POST 2.0/repositories/{workspace}/{repoSlug}
  SourceHost --> GitOps : repository
  CLI -> GitOps : create_service_repository(template_dir, service_request, repo_url)
  GitOps -> Template : render_cookiecutter_template(template_dir, service_request)
  Template -> Template : _safe_join rejects any rendered path outside the destination before the first mkdir
  Template --> GitOps : gitops_manifest_file set
  GitOps -> SourceHost : commit as PlatformBot and push the first commit
  SourceHost --> GitOps : pushed
end

group F-001-US6 — the availability tier alone fixes release strictness
  CLI -> Template : build_gitops_files(service_request)
  Template -> Profiles : read slo_profile and rollout_profile for the request's SLO class
  Profiles --> Template : slo_profile, rollout_profile
  Template -> Registry : look up cluster_entry for each target cluster
  Registry --> Template : cluster_entry
  Template --> CLI : gitops_manifest_file set for dev, staging and prod, in that order
end

group F-001-US4 — the infrastructure a service needs is proposed as its own reviewable change
  CLI -> CLI : partition the rendered set on the apps/{slug}/infra/ path segment
  CLI -> GitOps : stage_gitops_pr(branch seed/{slug}-infra-{issuekey}, infra gitops_manifest_file set)
  GitOps -> SourceHost : shallow clone, branch, remove the existing subtree for the slug, write, commit with the CI-skip marker, push
  GitOps -> SourceHost : POST 2.0/repositories/{workspace}/{repoSlug}/pullrequests
  SourceHost --> GitOps : gitops_pull_request
  GitOps --> CLI : gitops_pull_request
end

group F-001-US5 — the runtime declarations are proposed separately, covering every environment
  CLI -> CLI : partition the rendered set on the apps/{slug}/workload/ path segment
  CLI -> GitOps : stage_gitops_pr(branch seed/{slug}-workload-{issuekey}, workload gitops_manifest_file set for dev, staging and prod)
  GitOps -> SourceHost : POST 2.0/repositories/{workspace}/{repoSlug}/pullrequests
  SourceHost --> GitOps : gitops_pull_request
  GitOps --> CLI : gitops_pull_request
  CLI --> Requester : seed_result on stdout, exit 0
end

group F-001-US7 — see what a request would produce, and which cluster identity it would use, without touching anything
  Requester -> CLI : generate-gitops --service-name --slo-class --output-dir
  CLI -> Template : build_gitops_files(service_request)
  Template -> Profiles : slo_profile, rollout_profile
  Template -> Registry : cluster_entry
  Template --> CLI : gitops_manifest_file set written to the local output directory
  CLI --> Requester : exit 0, no tracker call and no source-host call
  Requester -> CLI : registry-show [name] or registry-paths
  CLI -> Registry : read the committed catalogue
  Registry --> CLI : cluster_entry records
  CLI --> Requester : cluster_entry records as JSON, or the catalogue path, exit 0
end

== Failure modes ==

group failure — a credential variable is absent
  CLI -> CLI : os.environ lookup by the configured variable name
  CLI --> Requester : error: environment variable {name} is not set, exit 2 before any network call
end

group failure — the issue type, key, name, slug or SLO class is unusable
  Intake --> CLI : JiraIntakeError carrying .field
  CLI --> Requester : exit 2 naming the field; no repository and no change set exist
end

group failure — the tracker is slow or unreachable
  CLI -> Tracker : GET rest/api/3/issue/{issueKey}
  Tracker --> CLI : no response within the 30 s urlopen bound
  CLI --> Requester : urlopen raises; the run stops with no partial state
end

group failure — the source host returns a 4xx that is not a repository conflict
  GitOps -> SourceHost : POST 2.0/repositories/{workspace}/{repoSlug}
  SourceHost --> GitOps : HTTPError
  GitOps --> CLI : RuntimeError naming method, path, status and body, never a credential
end

group failure — the repository already exists
  GitOps -> SourceHost : POST 2.0/repositories/{workspace}/{repoSlug}
  SourceHost --> GitOps : 400 carrying the repository-exists flag
  GitOps --> CLI : treated as success; the run continues to the template push
end

group failure — a rendered template path escapes the destination
  Template -> Template : _safe_join on every rendered path
  Template --> GitOps : raises with zero filesystem effect, before any mkdir or write
end

group failure — a template variable is undefined
  Template -> Template : Jinja2 StrictUndefined
  Template --> GitOps : raises at render; no gitops_manifest_file is produced
end

group failure — a tier profile is missing an SLO class
  Profiles --> Template : slo_profile or rollout_profile without one of bronze, silver, gold
  Template --> CLI : the module refuses to import, naming the missing classes
end

group failure — the requested cluster is not in the catalogue
  Template -> Registry : look up cluster_entry
  Registry --> Template : no such entry
  Template --> Requester : error: cluster not in registry, listing the known names, exit 2
end

group failure — a git subprocess hangs
  GitOps -> SourceHost : git clone, commit or push
  SourceHost --> GitOps : no response within the 300 s subprocess bound
  GitOps --> CLI : subprocess.TimeoutExpired raises
end

group failure — the cookiecutter binary is absent
  GitOps -> Template : render_cookiecutter_template
  Template -> Template : FileNotFoundError, fall back to the pure-Python renderer
  Template --> GitOps : gitops_manifest_file set, path safety still enforced
end

group failure — the run fails after the repository has been created
  CLI -> GitOps : a later step raises
  GitOps --> Requester : no compensating delete exists; the repository and any pushed commit remain, and re-running is the only recovery
end

note over CLI, GitOps
  invariants: DOM-001-R1, DOM-001-R2, DOM-001-R3, DOM-001-R4, DOM-001-R5, DOM-001-R6,
  DOM-001-R7, DOM-001-R8, DOM-001-R9, DOM-001-R10, DOM-001-R11, DOM-001-R12
  timeout 30000 ms per HTTP call, 300000 ms per git subprocess
  retry: none — a transient tracker or source-host failure fails the run
  idempotency: repository-exists tolerated; branch name seed/{slug}-{tier}-{issuekey};
  a re-seed replaces the service subtree rather than merging into it
  degraded: none — the run is not atomic across the tracker, the source host and the two change sets
end note

@enduml
